Package: GenE2scRNAseqIntro
Title: Introduction to Single-Cell RNA-seq Analysis with Bioconductor
Description:
    A live-coding workshop introducing single-cell RNA-seq analysis with
    Bioconductor, written for the Master 2 GenE2 "Single-Cell Omics and
    Spatial Transcriptomics" teaching unit. A short introduction explains how
    10x Genomics droplet-based experiments turn a tissue into a matrix of UMI
    counts. The 2h30 hands-on session then starts from the count matrix of the
    adult human testis (Guo et al. 2018, GEO accession GSE112013) and walks
    through the standard Bioconductor workflow: building a
    SingleCellExperiment, quality control, normalisation, feature selection,
    dimensionality reduction, batch correction, clustering, marker genes,
    reference-based annotation with SingleR and pseudobulk differential
    expression with DESeq2.
